Done. KLEE 3.2 is built from source against LLVM 16, with STP as its only solver and no uClibc.

**What was installed (all under `/usr/local`)**
| Component | Version / notes |
|---|---|
| minisat (stp fork) | static lib, `/usr/local/lib/libminisat.a` |
| STP | 2.3.4, `/usr/local/bin/stp`, `/usr/local/lib/libstp.a`, CMake config in `/usr/local/lib/cmake/STP` |
| KLEE | 3.2 (`92ee8201`), binaries `klee`, `klee-stats`, `klee-replay`, `klee-exec-tree`, `klee-zesti`; header `/usr/local/include/klee/klee.h`; runtimes `/usr/local/lib/klee/runtime` |

Build config: LLVM 16 (`/usr/lib/llvm-16`, `clang-16`), `-DENABLE_SOLVER_STP=ON`, Z3/metaSMT off, `ENABLE_KLEE_UCLIBC` off (uClibc runtime copy skipped), POSIX + KLEE-libc runtimes enabled. Sources and logs left at `/opt/build`.

**One source patch was required.** KLEE's `runtime/POSIX/fd.c` assumes x86 `__NR_*` syscall macros (`__NR_open`, `__NR_stat`, `__NR_access`, `__NR_chmod`, `__NR_chown`, `__NR_readlink`, `__NR_utimes`, `__NR_futimesat`, `__NR_select`), which don't exist on aarch64 — the build failed on them. I made each site fall back to the portable `*at` syscall family (`openat`, `newfstatat`, `faccessat`, `fchmodat`, `fchownat`, `readlinkat`, `utimensat`) when the legacy number is absent; original saved as `fd.c.orig`. This is an upstream portability gap, not something the STP/LLVM choices caused.

**Environment in `~/.bashrc`** — placed at the very top, *before* Ubuntu's `[ -z "$PS1" ] && return` guard, since the tests source it from a non-interactive shell: prepends `/usr/local/bin` to `PATH`, `/usr/local/include` to `CPATH`, `/usr/local/lib` to `LD_LIBRARY_PATH`, plus `KLEE_INCLUDE_DIR` and `KLEE_RUNTIME_LIBRARY_DIR`. Each is guarded so re-sourcing doesn't duplicate entries (backup at `~/.bashrc.bak-gnomon`).

**Verified** in a clean `env -i` shell sourcing `~/.bashrc`: `command -v klee` → `/usr/local/bin/klee`, `CPATH=/usr/local/include`, and a program including `<klee/klee.h>` compiled with plain `clang-16` (no `-I`) runs under `klee` reporting `Using STP solver backend` with the expected path/test counts; `klee-stats` also works.

